"1. The storage already matches Claude's model: DESIGN is a typed `Artifact` sharing versions, shares, library and sync (`prisma/schema.prisma:1344-1356`). The product around it is split into about ten \"made thing\" systems. One design has four editors with two save semantics, and no list shows everything Juno made.\n2. The worst defect is critical and confirmed by two independent browser repros: since `fb3a42b5` the app's enforcing CSP reaches the `srcdoc` sandbox (`src/middleware.ts:55-77`, `src/lib/csp.ts:31`). On the web, React, scripted HTML, Mermaid, the JS/Python console and public share previews are all dead.\n3. Design inside a conversation is broken on both platforms. On web, the chat Canvas editor remounts on an empty version after the first saved edit (`canvas-panel.tsx:1243-1253`; seven audits agree; I re-read it). On Mac, the dock cannot open any design made in chat (compact body in the message).\n4. Artifact lifetime is tied to chat messages:\n   - editing a message or regenerating hard-deletes artifacts, hand edits, design checkpoints and share links (`messages/[id]/route.ts:38-40`, `chat/route.ts:2566-2574`);\n   - model revisions overwrite user edits;\n   - a cut-off revision becomes current and is labelled \"verified\";\n   - deleting a conversation deletes hand-started designs.\n5. Designs grow 5 to 11 times after the size check and are stored above 200k characters. That blocks web editing, and because the native store fails closed on one bad or unknown record, it blanks the whole Mac and iPhone Artifacts and Design screens. This is the key blocker for adding Docs or Slides types.\n6. Mac design editing loses work: lost-update saves, `cornerSmoothing` stripped from every node, drafts dropped. The editor bundle shipped in 1.6.0 is stale (I ran `--check`: exit 1), its CSS lacks the shared primitives, and the inspector is hidden at the default window width.\n7. Work deliverables are a second, unmerged system. On web, .docx and .pptx can't be downloaded, tasks started on native are invisible, the iPhone's \"Made\" list is empty for cloud runs, and account deletion leaves the files in the bucket.\n8. Public links have no governance: bans don't reach shares, there is no takedown, no moderation, no quotas, and no telemetry. Moving previews to their own origin will re-enable scripts on share pages, so governance must ship in the same release.\n9. Scores (web/Mac): capability 6/4, UX 4/3, visual 7/5, motion 7/4, reliability 2/3, code health 6/5. Worth keeping: the validated operation layer, the patch protocol, stale-write guards, checked Office exports, one editor on all three platforms, and the sync and contract discipline.\n10. The merge is feasible and cheap at the data layer but should not start at the UI. The document lays out preconditions and URL and Mac-destination migrations in four steps:\n    - stop the bleeding (the fixes above);\n    - make artifacts first-class and stable, with soft delete;\n    - build one canonical route and one Artifacts list;\n    - add Claude-parity features: comments, links with access grants, phone editing, Docs and Slides.\n\nThe mac/liquid-glass-chat branch fixes none of the defects. I also checked one contradiction: the iPhone library can edit designs (`JunoMobileWorkspaceViews.swift:2062-2068`), so it is not read-only.\n\nFile: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/audit/00-AUDIT-OVERVIEW.md"